  "title": "Tab\u0101lu (region)",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/region"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The following places are located in Tabal: Artulu, Atunna, B\u012bt-Puruta\u0161, Hubu\u0161nu, Istuanda, Sinihtu, and *Tuhana. Tabal was briefly an Assyrian province during the reign of Sargon II (r. 721-705 BC), who conquered it 713 BC and lost it again two years later, in 711 BC.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Tabal is a region in the eastern and southeastern part of the central Anatolian high plateau (roughly the area of Cappadocia) and it is divided into several principalities (including B\u012bt-Puruta\u0161) and city-states.",
